    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d180">

                <pb facs="0306" n="212" sameAs="frus:frus1930v03/pg212"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">838.00 Elections/6:Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The High Commissioner in Haiti</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Russell</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting
                        Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Port-au-Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-03-20T12:00:00-05:00">March 20,
                        1930—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 5:42 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>38. Delegates of patriotic groups met at the Parisian, a theater, this morning
                    and selected Eugene Roy as their candidate for the <pb facs="0307" n="213"
                        xml:id="pg213"/> Presidency. Thirty-seven votes were for Roy, one
                        blank.<anchor n="20" xml:id="d180-f1"/> Announcement made from the platform
                    that Roy had been chosen in accordance with President Hoover’s plan as their
                    candidate for the Presidency.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Russell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d180-f1" n="20" xml:id="d180-f1-content">
                <p>A decree of nomination, dated March 20, 1930, stated that “out of thirty-four
                    votes citizen Eugene Roy has received thirty-four”. (838.00 Elections/16).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
